---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Docs" description="Getting started, publishing and format guidance for PlayMAKER, with availability clearly marked." path="/docs/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Guides & documentation</p><h1>Find your starting line.</h1><p class="section-lede">The site and pilot code are public. Product installation guides will grow as distributable releases become available.</p></div></section>
  <section class="page-section"><div class="shell copy-section">
    <div class="callout"><p><strong>Availability:</strong> WebMAKER is in pilot beta testing. TagMAKER and VideoMAKER are in early development. There are no standalone downloads to install from this site.</p></div>
    <h2 id="start">Start a first club</h2><ol><li>Explore the <a class="inline-link" href="/showcase/">Nerone Basket Anzio pilot</a> to understand the current WebMAKER scope.</li><li>Review the <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/mich1803/nerone-basket-anzio" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">pilot repository</a> for its own setup instructions and license before reusing code.</li><li>Define your club identity, content categories, match structure and publishing owner.</li><li>Follow project releases for a standalone WebMAKER setup guide. The pilot is not packaged as a general club installer.</li></ol>
    <h2 id="studio">Manage content with Studio</h2><p>WebMAKER Studio is a desktop publishing prototype in the roadmap. Its club onboarding, content editing and export steps will be documented when a public build is ready. For now, use the pilot repository's own documentation for any available workflow.</p>
    <h2 id="pages">Publish with GitHub Pages</h2><p>This <em>PlayMAKER organization site</em> is an Astro project. It is separate from the WebMAKER club product. To run this site locally:</p><pre><code>npm ci
npm run dev
npm run build</code></pre><p>For deployment, set the repository's <strong>Settings → Pages → Build and deployment → Source</strong> to <strong>GitHub Actions</strong>. A push to <code>main</code> builds and deploys the static <code>dist/</code> output. Pull requests build without deploying. See the repository README for the full checklist.</p>
    <h2 id="formats">Formats & data exchange</h2><p>No stable cross-product import/export contract is published yet. TagMAKER event exports and VideoMAKER imports are planned. Avoid building production integrations against an assumed schema; the versioned format guide will appear with working releases.</p>
    <h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Can I download all three apps today?</summary><p>No. The tools are in development, and there are no standalone releases linked from this site.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Does a club need AI or a subscription?</summary><p>The intended core workflows do not require mandatory AI services. This site has no subscription or account system.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Are all three products already integrated?</summary><p>No. Data interoperability is a roadmap goal. See the <a class="inline-link" href="/ecosystem/">ecosystem status</a>.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Where should I report an issue?</summary><p>Use Issues in the relevant public repository when enabled, or start from the <a class="inline-link" href={site.orgUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PlayMAKER organization</a>.</p></details>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
